{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured node1 with a hardened, chrooted Python web application running as locked, non-login account appsvc on TCP 8080. It starts automatically at boot and recovered successfully after a verified node reboot. RHEL 10.0, kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0, SELinux enforcing, SSH access, and protected configuration were preserved.","actions_performed":["Created locked system account appsvc with /sbin/nologin and no home directory.","Built a root-owned chroot using the already-installed Python 3.12 runtime; no OS or kernel upgrade was performed.","Installed root-owned application content and a hardened systemd service using RootDirectory=/srv/app-chroot.","Authorized TCP 8080 through SELinux and the active/permanent firewalld public zone.","Verified HTTP 200 behavior, appsvc UID/GID, zero capabilities, chroot confinement, and denied content writes and account login.","Rebooted node1 safely, observed a changed boot ID, and verified automatic service and data recovery.","Removed temporary test artifacts and repeated final HTTP, listener, SSH, and failed-unit checks."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Web application runs inside the chroot as unprivileged appsvc on port 8080","command_ids":["cmd-42a7d3fd29d14b94","cmd-c10f7cb675d6486c","cmd-f2d38bbae41a4de7","cmd-0972b5a336834c49"],"summary":"HTTP requests return 200 with the expected marker; the live process is UID/GID 992, has zero capabilities, and its root inode matches /srv/app-chroot. Only its Python process listens on port 8080."},{"requirement":"Starts at boot without an interactive login session","command_ids":["cmd-c10f7cb675d6486c","cmd-f0d4857898204c6f","cmd-f2d38bbae41a4de7","cmd-0972b5a336834c49"],"summary":"The unit is enabled and active after reboot with zero restarts and successful exit status. appsvc uses /sbin/nologin, has a locked password, no login audit session, and direct login is denied."},{"requirement":"Keep the installed OS release and kernel and use compatible software","command_ids":["cmd-45dcbb0485714fa2","cmd-d750d426dff545f0","cmd-aad4c515f79042a1","cmd-f2d38bbae41a4de7","cmd-f0d4857898204c6f"],"summary":"RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0 remained unchanged. The application uses the existing RHEL Python 3.12.9 runtime; the OS-release checksum was preserved."},{"requirement":"Security controls, administrative access, and cleanup","command_ids":["cmd-510095d0f469496b","cmd-7c2884886feb4ba1","cmd-f0d4857898204c6f","cmd-0972b5a336834c49"],"summary":"SELinux remains enforcing with no post-boot AVCs; 8080 is labeled http_port_t and allowed persistently by firewalld. SSH remains active with its configuration checksum unchanged, zero units are failed, and no test residue remains."},{"requirement":"node1 mandatory restart sequence","command_ids":["cmd-aad4c515f79042a1","cmd-69b45325647d4b6f","cmd-7ad48ec18e8a4a26","cmd-f2d38bbae41a4de7","cmd-0972b5a336834c49"],"summary":"Pre-restart boot ID and healthy service/data baseline were captured; the native safe reboot was acknowledged; the boot ID changed from 6ab6a71b-188c-48ae-971b-a6bb378b1d72 to 8e03a6dc-bac3-44e3-a72d-6ad0299b7b2a; service, content, HTTP response, listener, chroot identity, SSH, and system health recovered."}]}
